            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> What's needed here is really the union ([in the mathematical sense](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_(set_theory))) of the `cip` and `cii` text objects.\n\nIn mathematical sense it would intersection (\"region that part of `ip` AND `ii` regions\") and it was already discussed in #1233. It reasoning and resolution still stands: the \"no blanks indent scope\" textobject in practice is very often either `ip` or `ii`. Plus it is not really a good fit for 'mini.indentscope' as it has its own way of dealing with blank lines.\n\n> Maybe this is a case where a separate plugin for making textobjects based on set operations of other textobjects would be cool. It'd probably be more complicated than just making this though.\n\nThis is indeed a bit too much. The closest way to achieve this is by implementing custom 'mini.ai' textobject (I think computing an [array of regions](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5012cc35cebbdd97ab4f5906bcd713494d97b52e/doc/mini-ai.txt#L290-L310) will work nicely here).\n\nClosing as not planned.",
